= The Bureaucrats Strike

[? if bp_gov : **The Reorganisation.** Overnight, the Senate's administrative staff announce a "reorganisation of committee responsibilities". The Caucus's chairs are gone. Our people find their offices reassigned and their files transferred. The coalition carries on without us. "Nothing personal," a committee secretary explains. "The Senate must be governable." ?]

[? if bp_walkout : The [+ walkout_name +] will not take the Caucus back into government for at least a year. ?]

[? if bp_chancellor : **Valorum's fate.** A crisis breaks that the Chancellery seems to have heard about last: a shipping scandal, documents leaked to the HoloNet, a sector governor resigning in protest. Within days, the Senate is debating whether Chancellor [+ chancellor +] can still govern. ?]

[? if bp_fell : Our coalition partners do not wait to find out. One by one they withdraw their support, and the government of Chancellor [+ chancellor +] falls, exactly as Valorum's did. A new Chancellor will be elected, and the scandal will follow our candidate into the vote. ?][? if bp_saved : The constructive no-confidence rule saves the government: the plotters cannot agree on a successor, and the motion dies. ?]

The bureaucrats are satisfied, for now. *(The Senate bureaucracy is merely **cool** towards us again. [? if not constructive_vonc and rc_chancellor : A constructive no-confidence amendment would protect a Caucus Chancellor from this.?])*
